From 15a3c3c3b65d01009563cb02279cc5c978a64b07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:26:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Show the A-Z strip on the playlists listing

Every library listing with a name order has the strip except playlists, which kept
its header pinned but left the strip out. A library that mirrors a streaming account
can hold hundreds of playlists, so jumping to a letter matters there too. The server
already filters playlists by letter through the shared library_items query, and the
view already passes startsFrom/startsBefore along; only the switch was missing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/views/LibraryPlaylists.vue | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/views/LibraryPlaylists.vue b/src/views/LibraryPlaylists.vue
index b1ece83..994b4eb 100644
--- a/src/views/LibraryPlaylists.vue
+++ b/src/views/LibraryPlaylists.vue
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
     :load-paged-data="loadItems"
     :show-library="true"
     :sort-keys="sortKeys"
+    :show-alphabet-jump="true"
     :pin-listing-header="true"
     :update-available="updateAvailable"
     :title="$t('playlists')"
